      "deviations": [
        "tp_layer.cuh NOT reused for Mamba: it is decoder-wgmma-coupled (includes model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh, uses dectc::dectc_gemm_* and dec:: dims). The scan-dominated Mamba TC path projects with scalar owner-computes mb_linear, not wgmma tiles. Mamba therefore carries its OWN scalar TP helpers (mbtc:: in model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh) and reuses ONLY the transport-agnostic tp_transport.cuh + parallel_config.cuh — same as the decoder reuses for its math but with a Mamba-shaped partial.",
        "Attention head-shard does NOT apply (Mamba has no standard attention) — precisely scoped out per the task. The decoder's H_loc=kHeads/TP localization has no Mamba analogue.",
        "Mamba P1 is BATCH-PARALLEL SCALAR per-sample (mb_forward_sample/mb_backward_sample), NOT the decoder's wgmma grid-stride TILE loop. So the decoder C.3 grid-lockstep-over-TILES restructure was mirrored as grid-lockstep-over-SAMPLES (all CTAs cooperate on the same sample each round so tr.rendezvous(bar) is grid-uniform — the same §1 deadlock fix, applied to the scalar loop).",
        "SSM body (x_proj/dt/selective-scan, head-shared theta/B/C over Nc) is REPLICATED on the kTPComm path, not sharded: the Mamba SSM's head-shared terms do not decompose into independent per-rank channel shards the way per-head attention does. TP shards the projection RECOMBINATION boundaries only (out_proj+down fwd all-reduce; in_proj+gate/up dX bwd all-reduce) = the decoder's 4 reduce points minus the head localization. A full head-sharded selective scan is documented in-code as the deep follow-up.",
        "Per-rank weight shard (the host plan that makes TP numerically correct on real multi-GPU) is the upstream host plan (decoder E.3 parallel), out of this kernel track. The loopback exercises the publish/fixed-order-reduce MECHANISM; with replicated loopback weights it reduces P identical partials (the documented loopback artifact, noted in-code).",
        "2 pre-existing pytest failures are UNRELATED to TP and predate my edits (verified on the untouched baseline): test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands calls obsolete mod.tc_dump_outproj_operands (removed when Mamba moved to the scalar path); test_tc_single_step_grad_parity fails on layers.0.mixer.B_bias rel 1.55e-1 vs tol 0.08, which equals the bf16-vs-fp64 floor (1.546e-1) — a test tolerance-calibration issue, not a kernel bug. Both results are byte-identical before and after my edits.",
        "The worktree already contained a sibling ViT TP track (3 vit files, uncommitted/dirty) that mirrors the same decoder pattern; the prompt's commit message is literally 'vit/mamba TP track', so both were committed together. I verified the ViT TC TU compiles clean before committing."
